<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Technical Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all of our experiments, we use the same multi-view panorama generation model.
It was obtained via finetuning a pre-trained CubeDiff model, which itself is based on a variant of the popular Latent Diffusion Model architecture.
The finetuning uses the default diffusion loss for 90000 steps.
The learning rate is set to <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8e^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8e^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, with a linear ramp-up from 0 during the first 10000 steps.
During finetuning and inference of the model, we remove all text-conditioning.
Generating a single novel-view panorama with 50 diffusion steps takes around 30 seconds.
For MapAnything, we rely on the commercial checkpoint under Apache license.
To improve the visual quality of the renderings, we add a skybox texture to the 3DGS scene where MapAnything predicts infinite distance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Datasets</h2>

<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training data.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in the main paper, we adapt the Infinigen framework to procedurally generate synthetic multi-view panorama data, as can be seen in <a href="#A5.F10" title="In Rendering. ‣ Appendix E Evaluation Details ‣ Stepper: Stepwise Immersive Scene Generation with Multiview Panoramas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Indoor scenes are rooms of different categories (livingroom, bathroom, bedroom, kitchen, <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">etc</em>.<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>) and require about 1 hour to generate on a standard CPU machine.
Outdoor scenes are also sampled from different biomes (river, mountains, forest, cave, arctic, <em id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">etc</em>.<span id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span>).
However, due to them requiring more, complex assets like trees and bushes, their generation takes up to 3 hours on CPU.
In total, we generate 4730 indoor and 3252 outdoor scenes</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">During the generation process of a scene, a number of positions are sampled for panoramic cameras.
For an indoor scene, the pipeline places up to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=20</annotation></semantics></math> cameras at random locations in the room.
To reduce the numbers of assets that have to be generated to cover the bigger outdoor scenes, we only place <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math> cameras.
Sometimes, the placement algorithm can only find a smaller number of cameras.
For every placed camera, we render its view and the views <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=0.25m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=0.25m</annotation></semantics></math> to the right and to the left.
The two pairs <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[[\text{left},\text{center}],[\text{center},\text{right}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>left</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>center</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>center</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>right</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[[\text{left},\text{center}],[\text{center},\text{right}]]</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as the mirrored pair <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[[\text{center},\text{left}],[\text{right},\text{center}]]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>center</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>left</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext>right</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>center</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[[\text{center},\text{left}],[\text{right},\text{center}]]</annotation></semantics></math>, where we rotate the panorama by <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="180^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">180^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, are rendered.
Therefore, every placed camera yields <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=4</annotation></semantics></math> pairs of left-right panoramas with our desired baseline.
In total, we generate 187156 indoor and 49372 outdoor panorama pairs.
Due to the high resolution of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4096\times 2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4096</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4096\times 2048</annotation></semantics></math> and raytracing, the rendering process takes around 70 seconds per panorama on an A100 GPU.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28980v1/mapanything_ablation_comp.png" id="A4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:685/741;" width="685" height="741" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A4.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Impact of Multi-View Panoramas<span id="A4.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We depict the effect of using various options of panorama input for MapAnything and found that the auto-regressive expansion and sampling yield the most complete and accurate outputs.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Testing data.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We curate a test set of 16 synthetic scenes, for which we render an initial panorama and eight novel-view panoramas from different locations at a resolution of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4096\times 2048" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4096</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2048</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4096\times 2048</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each panorama, we also compute the corresponding depth map.
The scenes are obtained using Blender (6), Infinigen indoors (5) and Infinigen outdoors (5) and are visualized in <a href="#A5.F11" title="In Rendering. ‣ Appendix E Evaluation Details ‣ Stepper: Stepwise Immersive Scene Generation with Multiview Panoramas" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.
For the Blender scenes, we adapt the following sources, which are all under Creative Commons licenses:
Arctic ships<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://download.blender.org/archive/gallery/blender-splash-screens/blender-3-2/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://download.blender.org/archive/gallery/blender-splash-screens/blender-3-2/</a></span></span></span>,
Barbershop<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://svn.blender.org/svnroot/bf-blender/trunk/lib/benchmarks/cycles/barbershop_interior/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://svn.blender.org/svnroot/bf-blender/trunk/lib/benchmarks/
<br class="ltx_break">cycles/barbershop_interior/</a></span></span></span>,
Classroom<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://www.blender.org/download/demo-files/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://www.blender.org/download/demo-files/</a></span></span></span>,
Mountain cabin<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://www.blenderkit.com/get-blenderkit/28cb035a-d333-4e7f-a2b5-543629cdd982/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://www.blenderkit.com/get-blenderkit/28cb035a-d333-4e7f-a2b5-543629cdd982/</a></span></span></span>,
Valley<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://www.blenderkit.com/get-blenderkit/28cb035a-d333-4e7f-a2b5-543629cdd982/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://www.blenderkit.com/get-blenderkit/28cb035a-d333-4e7f-a2b5-543629cdd982/</a></span></span></span>,
Blue room<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://blog.polyhaven.com/blue-wall-scene-file/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://blog.polyhaven.com/blue-wall-scene-file/</a></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Qualitative examples.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We rely on a number of qualitative examples from other papers<span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://ys-imtech.github.io/projects/LayerPano3D/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://ys-imtech.github.io/projects/LayerPano3D/</a></span></span></span><span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            <a href="https://katjaschwarz.github.io/worlds/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://katjaschwarz.github.io/worlds/</a></span></span></span> to demonstrate the generalization capabilities of our method.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28980v1/supp_unrolling_comp.png" id="A4.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/520;" width="685" height="520" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A4.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Auto-regressive steps.<span id="A4.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We perform a number of auto-regressive steps to generate novel-view panoramas from the initial panorama to the left and right for several examples. From the generated panoramas, we visualize the forward-facing view to highlight the generated details. A single step corresponds to a step length of <math id="A4.F9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Evaluation Details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For every test scene, we generate a 3DGS scene with every baseline.
As a first step, we transform every scene such that its scene origin and rotation line up with the ground-truth scene.
This can be achieved using the camera configurations from the individual reconstructions.
Then, we align the scale of every scene with the scale of the ground-truth scale.
To this end, we render a depth map in all four horizontal directions with a 90 degree field-of-view and a resolution of <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024\times 1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024\times 1024</annotation></semantics></math> for the initial panorama (at the origin of the scene).
After filtering out invalid depths, the scene scale is determined via the median of all scales between the rendered and ground-truth depths.
Our scenes tend to contain around <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.5\times 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.5\times 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> Gaussians, Matrix-3D’s scenes around <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\times 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\times 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> Gaussians, LayerPano3D’s scenes around <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> Gaussians, and WorldExplorer’s scenes around <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.4\times 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.4\times 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> Gaussians.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rendering.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using the alignment and scaling from above, we render the six cubefaces for each of the 9 panorama (initial + 8 novel-view panoramas) with a field of view of 90 degrees and a resolution of <math id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024\times 1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024\times 1024</annotation></semantics></math> once from the 3DGS scene and once from the ground-truth panoramas using resampling.
The 3DGS rendering is performed using the open-source <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gsplat</span> library.
For every rendered cubeface (54 in total), we compute the NVS metrics SSIM, LPIPS, and PSNR and report the average.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28980v1/data_comp.png" id="A5.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/457;" width="685" height="457" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A5.F10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Multi-view panoramas pairs generated with Infinigen.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28980v1/data_test_comp.png" id="A5.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/352;" width="685" height="352" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A5.F11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Input panoramas used for testing.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.28980v1/imgs_supp_v2/user_study_comp.jpg" id="A5.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:685/1212;" width="685" height="1212" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A5.F12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">User study form.<span id="A5.F12.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Participants fill out this randomized form and cast a single vote per category.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
